# Design system: tokens and styling

## Values are defined centrally, never inline

Any value that *means* something is defined once and referenced by name — even
with one reference today. By kind:

- **Design values** (color, spacing, radius, type, z-index, motion) → a token in
  `design-system/v2/tokens/`.
- **Designed non-token constants** → `tokens/component.css`, per band only
  where used. Constants that reference `--t` or the weights are declared on
  `.page`, never `:root` (a custom property resolves its inner `var()`s where
  it is declared).
- **Per-island magic numbers** (timings, thresholds, beat positions) → a
  named-constants block at the top of the island file.
- **Repeated CSS values** → a custom property referenced everywhere.
- **Copy, labels, URLs, asset paths, endpoints** → a `*-data.ts` module, the
  media registry, or `.env` (see `60-data-and-integrations.mdc`).

The test: if another file could ever need to agree on the value, or a reader
would ask "why this number?", it gets a central name.

## Styling lives in the token layers

- Reference the custom properties from `tokens/` for every color, font,
  radius, spacing, z, and motion value. No hardcoded hex or magic px in
  component CSS.
- Structure rides the grid: ticks, weights, em at anchor ratios, or fixed
  material px per band — see `30-grid-and-layout.mdc`.
- Every hex color is a token named by role, not hue. The two commented
  cold-load literals in the root layout (guard style, theme-color) are the
  standing exceptions.
- `!important` is forbidden. Fix the cascade. The base reset's `[hidden]` is
  the one exception.
- If a literal appears twice with the same design intent, promote it to a
  custom property. Two copies always drift.
- Type is set through the `--ts-*` tokens: `font`, `letter-spacing`,
  `font-variation-settings: "opsz" …, var(--font-sans-slnt)`,
  `font-optical-sizing: none`, and `text-transform` where the token carries a
  case. Never a bare `font-size`.

Inline `style={{}}` is allowed only for: forwarding a per-instance value the
CSS cannot know (a color role, a frame index); CSS custom properties consumed
by a stylesheet rule (`style={{ '--gx': n }}`, `setProperty("--eng-x", …)`);
transient animation state (`willChange`). A value that never changes per
instance belongs in a class.

## The z-index scale

Tokens in `tokens/component.css`: `--z-base` · `--z-raised` · `--z-sticky` ·
`--z-nav` · `--z-modal` · `--z-portal`. Anything that stacks against the rest
of the page uses a token. Inside one isolated stacking context, siblings may
use `1/2/3`. No raw numbers above `3` in component files.

## Motion grammars

Motion is a vocabulary of named CSS grammars in `tokens/motion.css` — each
defined in prose in the file (draw-down, fade-rise, the chip wipe, the
carousel slide). No animation runtime ships.

- Reuse before inventing. A new grammar is named and defined in prose first.
- Constants are born in `component.css` and promote to `motion.css` at their
  second consumer, values unchanged, prior names becoming aliases. Alias
  curves; never fork them.
- Opens run the ease-in-out curve; closes run the ease-out. A hard shadow never
  paints while its box moves: the offset grows from 0,0 after the box lands
  and drops at once on close.
- Choreographies settle: a load choreography ends its run explicitly on the
  final beat's `animationend`, so band-gated variants never replay motion on
  resize.
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` renders every grammar state-to-state — no
  transitions, no timers, elements born settled. A no-JS render shows the same
  settled state.
- Hover styles sit under `@media (hover: hover)`; every state also works on
  touch.

## CSS transition constraints

- Colors do not transition on gradients; transition the opacity of an absolute
  child that carries the gradient.
- An inline `style` color overrides a CSS color transition; apply the inline
  style only while active.
- Never start a `translate`/transform transition inside an element whose paint
  is transitioning — the compositor layer re-rasters the ancestor mid-paint
  (a one-frame flicker `will-change` does not fix). Animate a paint-in-place
  offset (relative `left`) for small moves. `translate` is fine where no
  ancestor paint transitions.
- Use a CSS `filter` for desaturation on anything whose background transitions;
  `mix-blend-mode: luminosity` interacts badly with it.

## Fonts are licensed

**GT Standard Standard VF** and **PP Kyoto Variable Upright** are licensed and
not on any public CDN. Never `@import` them from a URL; never commit them to a
public mirror. Files live in `public/media/fonts/`, loaded by `@font-face` in
`tokens/fonts.css` and preloaded by the root layout. GT Standard's variable
default weight is 900: every style sets an explicit weight or text renders
Black. The per-step optical-size pins live in `tokens/type.css`, generated by
`scripts/generate-v2-type-css.mjs` from `tokens/type-styles.json` — edit the
JSON and regenerate; never hand-edit the generated block.

## SVG and icons

- Vector geometry is never hand-authored. Icons and marks are exported
  verbatim from Figma through the console bridge; the only permitted edit is
  normalizing paint to `currentColor` where the icon tints with text.
- Shapes with no vector geometry — dots, plain circles and squares, corner
  triangles — are CSS with token fills, not files.
- Never export with Figma's Exclude / Boolean Subtract; ask for a flattened
  re-export (background as one `<path>`, foreground as separate paths with
  explicit fills).
- Threshold: used once and ≤ ~20 lines → inline in the component; used twice
  anywhere → `v2/icons.tsx` with `color`/`size` props; complex artwork → a
  file in `public/media/` registered in `v2/media.ts`. SVG markup appears in
  source exactly once.

## Images are art-directed tier sets

Photography renders as `<picture>` with one media-gated `<source>` per width
tier and the smallest tier as the `<img>` fallback. Tier cuts follow the
structural gates; cut each at 2× its band's rendered frame. Explicit
`width`/`height` on every image; WebP only; `alt=""` for ambient photography.
The deploy serves static assets directly (`images.unoptimized`) — the tier
markup is the delivery mechanism.

## Public assets and the media registry

Static media lives under `public/media/`, organized by function
(`hero-carousel/`, `portfolio/`, `engines/`, `testimonials/`, `brand/`,
`fonts/`). Only favicons, `og-image.png`, and `site.webmanifest` sit at the
public root.

`design-system/v2/media.ts` is the single source of truth mapping every asset
to its path with a typed descriptor. Code never hardcodes an asset path. The
only literal paths are the contexts that cannot import TS: `@font-face` in
`fonts.css`, the root layout's preload hrefs, and app metadata.

Names are lowercase kebab-case, most general to most specific, identifiable
without opening the file. Match the folder's existing pattern. Delete replaced
assets and their registry entries.
